*  M1-R4b witness: a function DEFINE'd TWICE is legal SPITBOL (last DEFINE wins).
*  m4 emitted a face label per DEFINE site, so `as` rejected `F_α` defined twice.
        DEFINE('F(x)')                                                                       :(FEnd)
F       F          =     'got:' x                                                            :(RETURN)
FEnd
        DEFINE('F(x)')
        OUTPUT     =     F('one')
        OUTPUT     =     F('two')
END
